Research in the twentieth-century has shown that there are two pools of genetic variations: hidden and expressed.
Mutation provides for new genetic variations and selection removes these variations expressed from the pool.
Segregation and recombination mix back and forth the variation between the two pools with each generation.
Outside in the savannah it is difficult for a primate with a digestive system such as the human to meet his need for amino acid from available plant sources.
In addition, it has serious consequences if one refrains: growth depression, malnutrition and ultimately death.
The most easily accessible plant resources would have been the proteins in leaves and legumes, but these are difficult to digest for primates like us, unless they are cooked.
In contrast, animal food sources (ants, termites, eggs) are not only easily digestible, but also provide large amounts of proteins that contain all essential amino acids.
Overall, it shouldn’t surprise us if our own ancestors solved their “protein problem” in a similar way the chimpanzees in the savannah do today.
Sleeping sleep subsidence is the process of targeted waking up during normal sleep periods and falling asleep for a short time (10-60 minutes) later.
This can be easily achieved by using a relatively quiet alarm clock to bring you to consciousness without completely arousing you.
If you’re someone who introduces the alarm clock in your sleep, you can put it on the other side of the room so that you’re compelled to leave the bed to turn it off.
Another biorhythm-based possibility is to drink a lot of fluids before bed (especially water or tea, which is known for its diuty effect), so you are forced to stand up for urination.
The measure of inner calm that a man possesses correlates in reverse with the measure of tension in body and mind.
The lower the tension, the more positive the existing life force is. Every person has the potential to find absolute rest and satisfaction.
Anyone can attain enlightenment. The only thing that stands in the way of this goal is our own tension and negativity.
Tibetan Buddhism is based on the teachings of Buddha, but has been extended to include the path of Mahayana’s love and numerous techniques of Indian yoga.
In principle, Tibetan Buddhism is very simple. It consists of Kundalini yoga, meditation and the path of all-encompassing love.
Kundalini yoga awakens the Kundalini energy through yoga poses, breathing exercises, mantras and visualizations.
At the center of Tibetan meditation is god-yoga. Through the visualization of various deities, the energy channels are purified, the chakras are opened and the enlightened consciousness arises.
Germany was a common enemy in World War II, resulting in co-operation between the USSR and the U.S
Two years after the end of the war, the former Allies were now enemies and the Cold War began.
He was to last for the next 40 years and, in reality, be held by proxy armies on battlefields from Africa to Asia, Afghanistan, Cuba and many other places.
On 17 September 1939, the Polish defense had already completely collapsed and the only hope was a retreat and a re-establishment along the Romanian bridgehead.
However, these plans became obsolete almost overnight when over 800,000 soldiers of the Red Army of the Soviet Union invaded the Belarusian and Ukrainian fronts and created them after they invaded the eastern regions of Poland in violation of the peace treaty of Riga, the Soviet-Polish non-aggression pact and other bilateral and multilateral international treaties.
The use of ships for freight transport is by far the most efficient method for transporting large quantities of people and goods across the oceans.
The mission of the Navy has traditionally been to ensure that a country remains capable of transporting people and goods, and at the same time impeding the enemy’s ability to transport people and goods.
One of the most significant newer examples of this is the North Atlantic campaign in World War II. The Americans tried to bring workforce and material across the Atlantic Ocean to help Britain.
At the same time, the German navy tried to stop this traffic mainly with submarines.
If the Allies had failed, Germany could probably have conquered Britain just like the rest of Europe.
Goats appear to have been domesticated about 10,000 years ago in Zāgros mountains in Iran.
Antique cultures and folk tribes began to keep them as farm animals in order to easily get their milk, fur, meat and skin.
House goats were usually kept in herds that wandered on hills or other pastures. The goats were supervised by goat herders, very similar to the better-known shepherds; often these were children or adolescents. These grazing procedures are still used today.
Already in the 16th century they built conveyor tracks in England.
Although the conveyor tracks consisted only of parallel wooden boards, they allowed the horses, which drew the wagons, to reach higher speeds and draw greater loads than on the slightly rougher roads of that time.
Thresholds were introduced quite early in order to secure the position of the rails, but little by little the realization prevailed that rails, which carry a ribbon made of iron, are more efficient.
This became commorable, but the iron caused more wear on the wooden wheels of the cars.
Finally, the wooden wheels were replaced by iron wheels. In 1767, the first completely iron rails were introduced.
The first known mode of locomotion was walking. Man began two million years ago with the advent of Homo Erectus (which means “uprighting man”) to go upright.
Their predecessors, the Australopithecus, didn't go upright so regularly.
Two-footed species are found in Australopithecus fossils from 4.2 to 3.9 million years ago, although Sahellanthropus may have already walked on two legs as early as seven million years ago.
