It is really obvious that the world has changed a lot due to the scientific and technological advances of humanity and that the problems have become more serious due to overpopulation and the extravagant way of life of the people.
After its passage by Congress on July 4, a hand-written draft signed by Congress President John Hancock and Secretary Charles Thomson has been sent a few blocks away to John Dunlap's printing house.
Over the course of the night, between 150 and 200 copies were made, which are now known as “Dunlapsides”.
John Nixon gave the first public reading of the document at Independence Hall's courtyard on July 8.
One was sent to George Washington on July 6, who read it aloud to his troops in New York on July 9. A copy reached London on August 10.
The 25 Dunlap pages that still exist are the oldest remaining copies of the document. The original manuscript did not outlast the times.
Many paleontologists nowadays believe that there is a group of dinosaurs that have survived and are still alive today. We call them birds.
Many don't see them as dinosaurs because they have feathers and can fly.
Yet many things about birds still look like a dinosaur.
They have feet with dandruff and claws, laying eggs and running on both hind legs like a Tyrannosaurus rex.
Almost all computers used today are based on the processing of information encoded in the form of binaries.
A binary number can have only one of two values, namely 0 or 1, and these numbers are referred to as binary digits—or as bits to use the computer jargon.
Internal poisoning may not be detected immediately. The symptoms, such as vomiting, are so general that you cannot immediately make a diagnosis.
The best sign of intoxication caused by swallowing can be the presence of an open container with medication or toxic household chemicals.
Look on the label for specific first aid instructions for this particular poison.
The term “bug” is used by entomologists in a formal sense for this insect group.
This term derives itself from the ancient familiarity with bed bugs. These are insects that are very adaptable in parasitizing humans.
Both predators and bed bugs are nidicol, i.e. adapted to living in the nest or housing their hosts.
In the United States of America, there are about 400,000 known cases of multiple sclerosis (MS), making it the most prevalent neurological disease in younger and middle-aged adults.
MS is a disease that impairs the central nervous system composed of the brain, spinal cord, and ophthalmic nerve.
Research has shown that in women the probability of developing MS is twice as high as in men.
A couple may decide that it is not in their own interest or in the interest of their child to raise a baby.
These couples can opt for an adoption plan for their baby.
In the case of an adoption, the biological parents give up their parental rights, so that another couple can take parenthood.
Science’s main objective is to use the scientific method to find out how the world works. This method is indeed the basis of most scientific investigations.
However, it’s not just about experimentation, with an experiment being a test designed to exclude one or more of the possible hypotheses. Scientific research is also guided by asking questions and conducting observations.
