Many observed rhythms in physiology and behavior are often largely based on the presence of the body’s own cycles and their production by biological clocks.x
Behaviors determined by a cycle, which are not only reactions to signs of external cycles, are known in most organisms, including bacteria, fungi, plants and animals.
Biological clocks are self-sustaining oscillators, which even in the absence of external signals perform free-swinging cycles.
Hershey-Chase experiment was one of the most authoritative circumstantial circumstantial evidence that DNA is a genetic material.
Hershey and Chase used phages or viruses to incorporate their own DNA into a bacterium.
They carried out two experiments in which they labeled either radioactive phosphorus phage DNA or a protein in phages with radioactive sulphur.
Mutations can have a wide variety of effects depending on what kind of mutation it is, the significance of the relevant piece of genetic material and whether the cells in question are germline cells.
Only mutations in germline cells can be transmitted to children, while mutations elsewhere can lead to cell death or cancer.
Close-to-nature tourism attracts people who are interested in visiting natural areas to enjoy the countryside, including wild plants and animals.
Examples of on-site activities include hunting, fishing, photography, bird watching, visiting parks, and learning information about the ecosystem.
An example of this is the visit, photography and study of orangutangs in Borneo.
Every morning people leave small provincial towns by car to drive to their workplace and are passed by others whose place of work is in the place they've just left.
In this dynamic commute, everyone is, in some ways, connected to a transport system based on the private passenger car, and support it.
Science now points out that this massive carbon economy has released the biosphere from one of its stable states that human evolution has sustained over the past two million years.
Everyone participates in the company and uses transport systems. Almost everyone complains abount the transport systems.x
In developed countries, you will rarely hear a similar number of complaints about the water quality or the collapse of bridges.
Why do transport systems lead to such grievances, why do they fail on a day-to-day basis? Are traffic engineers simply incompetent? Or is there something more fundamental here?
Traffic flow is an examination of the movement of individual drivers and vehicles between two points and the interactions that take place between the two.
Unfortunately, the study of traffic flows is difficult, as driver behavior cannot be predicted with one hundred percent safety.
Fortunately, motorists tend to behave reasonably consistently; therefore, traffic flows have a certain consistency and can be represented mathematically roughly.
In order to better represent the flow of traffic, the correlations between the three most important properties were defined: (1) flow, (2) density and (3) speed.
These relationships help with the planning, design and operation of facilities on the roadway.
Insectors were the first animals to conquer the skies. Their ability to fly helped them dodge enemies more easily and find efficient food and sex partners.
Most insectors can fold their wings back along their bodies.
As a result, they have a broader selection of small shelters where they can hide from predators.
Today, dragonflies and one-day flies are the only insectors who can't fold their wings back.
Thousands of years ago, a man named Aristarch claimed that the sun was at the heart of the solar system's movements.
Some people thought he was right, but many believed the opposite: that the solar system, including the sun (and even the other stars), was moving around the Earth.
This seems reasonable, since it doesn’t seem like the earth is moving, right?
The Amazon is the second longest and the most water-rich river on earth. It runs more than eight times like water like the second-largest stream.
The Amazon is also Earth's widest river, sometimes up to six miles wide.
20 percent of the water that flows into the oceans via the rivers of the planet comes from the Amazon.
The main stream is 6387 km (3980 miles) long. It absorbs water from thousands of smaller rivers.
Although the construction of stone pyramids was continued until the end of the Old Empire, the pyramids of Giza were never surpassed in size and the technical perfection of their construction.
Egyptians in the ancient New Kingdom marveled at the monuments of their ancestors, who were a good thousand years old at that time.
The Vatican City has about 800 inhabitants. It is the smallest independent state in the world and the country with the smallest population.
Vatican City uses Italian for its legislation and official communications.
Italian is also the everyday language of most who work in the state, while Latin is often used in religious ceremonies.
All citizens of Victain City are Roman-Catholic.
Basic chemical elements such as gold, silver and copper have been known to humans since antiquity, as these can all be found in nature in their original form and degraded with primitive tools.
Aristoteles, a philosopher, put forward the theory that all things consist of a mixture of one or more of four elements. These were earth, water, air and fire.
This corresponded more to the four states of aggregation (in the same order): solid, liquid, gas and plasma. However, he also established the theory that they turn into new substances to form what we see.
Alloys are basically a mixture of two or more metals. Don’t forget that there are many elements in the periodic table.
Elements such as calcium and potassium are regarded as metals. Of course, there are also other metals such as silver and gold.
There are also alloys containing small amounts of non-metallic elements such as carbon.
