The effectiveness of filters varies greatly, and if you have concerns, then you should consider buying your water in a sealed bottle from a reputable company.
Travelers can come across animal pests they don't know from their home regions.
Vermin can destroy food, cause irritation or, at worst, even trigger allergic reactions, administer poison or transmit diseases.
Infectious diseases as such or dangerous animals, which can injure or kill people by force, are usually not classified as vermin.
Duty-free shoulding is the ability to purchase goods that are exempt from levies and excise duties in certain places.
Travelers whose destination country has high taxation can sometimes save a significant amount of money, especially on products such as alcoholic beverages and tobacco.
The section between Point Marion and Fairmount on Buffalo-Pittsburgh Highway is arguably the biggest driving challenge, as it often runs through remote, untapped terrain.
If you’ren’t used to driving on country roads, you’ll stay careful: steep gradients, narrow lanes and sharp curves predominate here.
The specified speed limits are noticeably lower than in the previous and subsequent sections - usually 35-40 mph (56-64 km/h) - and their strict adherence is even more important than usual.
Yet interestingly, mobile coverage here is much better than in many other areas of the track, such as the Pennsylvania Wilds.
German baked goods are quite delicious. In Bavaria they are quite rich and varied, as well as with the southern neighbor Austria.
Fruit pastries are widespread, with apples cooked all year for pastries and cherries and plums used in summer.
Many German baked goods also contain almonds, hazelnuts or other nuts. Popular cakes often go particularly well with a cup of strong coffee.
If you want to make small but rich baked goods, then try what, depending on the region, is referred to as Berliner, pancakes or doughnuts.
A curry is a dish based on herbs and spices, along with either meat or vegetables.
A curry can be either “dry” or “moist” depending on the amount of liquid.
Yogurt is commonly used in curries in the inland of northern India and Pakistan; coconut milk is commonly used in southern India and several other coastal regions of the subcontinent.
With a selection of 17,000 islands, Indonesian food is an umbrella term that includes a wide variety of regional kitchens found throughout the country.
However, if the term is used without other attributes, it usually refers to the food that originally comes from the central and eastern parts of the main island of Java.
Javanian cuisine, which is now spread all over the archipelago, offers a variety of simply seasoned dishes. As flavor carriers, the Javaneses prefer peanuts, chillies, sugar (particularly Javanian coconut blossom sugar) and a range of aromatic spices.
Stirrups are aids for the rider's feet hanging down on both sides of the saddle.
They give more stability to the rider, but there are safety concerns, because the rider’s feet can possibly get caught up in them.
If a rider falls from the horse and catches himself with the foost at the stirrup, he can be dragged along if the horse goes through. To keep this risk as low as possible, a number of safety precautions can be taken.
First of all, most riders wear riding boots with a heel and a sleazy, quite narrow sole.
In addition, some saddles, in particular English saddles, have safety brackets, which make it possible for a stirrup belt to fall off the saddle as soon as it is pulled backwards by a plunging rider.
Cochamó Valley – Chile’s main climbing destination, known as Yosemite National Park of South America, with a variety of large granite walls and cliffs.
The summits offer a breathtaking view. Climbers from all over the world are constantly discovering new routes along the walls that offer endless possibilities.
Downhill sports such as skiing and snowboarding are popular sports, where skis or a snowboard are attached to your feet and a slope down over a snow-covered surface.
Skiing is a popular travel activity with many enthusiasts, occasionally also known as “Skipenners”, who are planning their entire holiday around skiing in a certain place.
The idea of skiing is very old – cave paintings with depictions of skiers go back to 5000 BC!
The origins of ski descent as a sport date back at least to the 17th century and in 1861 the first recreational ski club in Australia was opened by Norwegians.
Ski hiking with a backpack: This activity is also known as ski touring or ski hiking.
It is similar to alpine touring or mountaineering, but it does not necessarily include them, since the latter are carried out in steep terrain and require much firmer skis and boots.
Look at the ski route as a similar walking route.
In good conditions, you’ll be able to cover slightly longer distances than when you’re hiking – you’ll very rarely reach the speed from cross-country skiing on well-kept cross-country ski trails without a heavy backpack.
Europe is a relatively small continent, but has numerous independent countries. Normally, you would have to apply for visas several times and go through several passport checks if you want to travel through several countries.
In this regard, however, the Schengen area functions a little like a country.
As long as you stay in this zone, you can usually cross the boundaries without having to go through the passport control again.
Correspondingly, you do not have to apply for a visa for each of the Schengen member countries individually, which saves time, money and bureaucracy.
There is no universal definition of which manufactured objects are considered antiquities. Some tax authorities define over 100-year-old goods as antiquities.
The definition has geographical deviations where the age limit may be lower in areas such as North America than in Europe.
Handmade products could be described as ‘antiquity’, even though they are younger than similar mass-produced products.
Reindeer breeding is an important source of Sámi's livelihood, and the culture around trade is also important for many who work in other professions.
Even in the past, not all sámi have breed reindeer on a large scale, but have lived from fishing, hunting and the like. Reindeer kept them mainly as draught animals.
Today many Sámi work in modern professions. Tourism is an important source of income in Sápmi, the Sámi region.
