The views presented are often superficial, general and too much simplified in comparison to the more detailed information found elsewhere.
Severe weather is the collective term for any dangerous weather phenomenon with the potential to cause damage, serious social disturbances or the loss of human lives.
Severe weather can occur anywhere in the world and there are different types of it that depend on geography, topography and atmospheric conditions.
Strong winds, hail, excessive rainfall and wildfires are shapes and effects of storms, as are thunderstorms, tornadoes, water pants and cyclones.
Regional and seasonal severe weather phenomena include blizzards, snowstorms, ice storms and dust storms.
Travellers are urgently cautioned to pay attention to any kind of severe weather affected by their area, as this may affect all travel plans.
Anyone planning to travel to a country that is considered a war zone should undergo professional training for it.
