Crack currents are the returning stream of waves broken on the beach, often in reefs or the like.
Due to the underwater topology, the reflux is concentrated in a few deeper areas and a fast flow up to deep water can form there.
Most deaths are caused by obsoletion in attempting to swim back against the current, which may prove impossible.
Coming out of the current, swimming back is not more difficult than normal.
Try to get somewhere where you won’t get caught again. Alternatively, depending on your skills and depending on whether you’ve been noticed, you might want to wait for rescue.
