Other islands include Livingston Island and Deception, where the flooded caldera of a still-active volcano features a spectacular natural harbor.
Ellsworthland is the region south of the peninsula bordered by Lake Bellingshausen.
The mountains of the peninsula merge into the plateau here and then rise again to form the 360 km chain of the Ellsworth mountains, which is divided into two by the Minnesota Glacier.
