Barcelona’s official languages are Catalan and Spanish. Roughly half of the inhabitants prefer to speak Catalan, the vast majority understand it, and almost everyone can speak Spanish.
Most signs, however, are indicated only in Catalan, as it is stipulated by law as the first official language.
Nevertheless, Spanish is also widely used in public transport and other facilities.
Normal announcements take place in the metro exclusively in Catalan, but unforeseen faults are reported by an automated system in a variety of languages, including Spanish, English, French, Arabic and Japanese.
