In Christianity, Christmas is one of the most important holidays and is the birthday of Jesus.
Many of the traditions around the festival have also been adopted by non-believers in Christian and non-Christian countries all over the world.
There's the tradition of spending Easter night awake in some vacancy to see the sunrise.
There are, of course, Christian-theological explanations for this tradition, but it could also be a pre-Christian spring and fertility ritual.
More traditional churches often hold an Easter Wake on Saturday evenings, during the Easter weekend, with the celebrations of the congregations often beginning at midnight, where the resurrection of Christ is celebrated.
