This provides a good opportunity to see the Northern Lights as the sky is darken more or less around the clock.
Since the areas are sparsely populated and light pollution is therefore often no problem, you can also enjoy the starry sky.
Japan's work culture is more hierarchical and formal than what Westerners may be used to.
Suits belong to the common business clothes and colleagues address each other with their family names or activity designations.
Harmony in the workplace is of crucial importance, with the focus being on group performance rather than the praise for individual achievements.
Employees often have to seek the consent of their superiors for all the decisions they make and they are expected to unconditionally follow the instructions of their bosses.
